_genai_extension.py,venv/Lib/site-packages/langchain_google_genai/_genai_extension.py,f7b39163b51628fe6025c1275dab419621c55b41,sudofixit/scraper,https://api.github.com/repositories/960689798/contents/venv/Lib/site-packages/langchain_google_genai/_genai_extension.py?ref=a9ea19ba490a39de8b8d59eb8fd32d2c6e50b99d,https://api.github.com/repositories/960689798/git/blobs/f7b39163b51628fe6025c1275dab419621c55b41,https://github.com/sudofixit/scraper/blob/a9ea19ba490a39de8b8d59eb8fd32d2c6e50b99d/venv/Lib/site-packages/langchain_google_genai/_genai_extension.py,,,0,0,0,10,2025-05-07T20:47:51Z,0,0,"🚀 CUD Course Scraper: AI-Powered & Student-Friendly
Scrape course schedules in 2 clicks—no coding needed. Perfect for students who want to:

✅ Auto-login to the CUD portal

📅 Find classes by professor/term

📥 Export to CSV (for Excel/Google Sheets)

🌟 Why Use This?
AI does the work: A bot mimics how you browse—clicks buttons, fills forms, scrapes data.

No tech skills needed: Just enter your student ID/password.

Instant filters: See which professors teach what, when.

App Demo

🛠️ Setup (5 Minutes)

git clone https://github.com/sudofixit/scraper 
cd scraper 
pip install -r requirements.txt  

Get a free Google Gemini API Key 

Create .env file in the project folder:

ID = ""20240001234""          # Auto-updates in the app   
PASSWORD = ""••••••••""       # Auto-updates in the app  
GEMINI_API_KEY = ""AIzaSy...""# Paste Gemini key here  
TERM = ""71""                 # Auto-updates in the app  
🖥️ How to Run
Open the app:


streamlit run app.py  
In the browser:

Enter ID + password

Choose a term (e.g., ""FA 2024-25"")

Click ""Start Scraping""

Wait 1-2 mins (watch the bot work in Chrome!)

Done! Filter courses or download CSV.

🔧 Troubleshooting


""Invalid login""	Double-check ID/password in .env

